Fix the IL2087 and IL2090 AOT/trim warnings in the following files in `/tmp/sv-ae77b457450e4df2a3d754e10c8d8cf0/before/`. Do NOT use `#pragma warning disable` or `[UnconditionalSuppressMessage]`.

## 1. GenericOperationSource.cs

The class `GenericOperationSource<T>` uses reflection on `typeof(T)`:
- Line 37: `ModelReaderWriter.Read(response.Content, typeof(T))` — IL2087 because T needs `PublicConstructors | NonPublicConstructors`  
- Line 40: `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), BindingFlags.NonPublic | BindingFlags.Instance, ...)` — IL2087 because T needs `NonPublicConstructors`

Fix: Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]` constraint on T in the class declaration:
```csharp
internal class GenericOperationSource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T> : IOperationSource<T>
```

## 2. ArmOperation.cs

The method `IsResource<T>()` at lines 96-111 uses:
- Line 98: `typeof(T).GetConstructor(BindingFlags.NonPublic | BindingFlags.Instance, ...)` — IL2090
- Line 104: `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), BindingFlags.NonPublic | BindingFlags.Instance, ...)` — IL2087

Fix: Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]` to the T type parameter on the `IsResource<T>()` method:
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>() where T : notnull
```

Also, look at where `IsResource<T>()` is called (should be around line 50 and line 88). The callers `Rehydrate<T>` and `RehydrateAsync<T>` need to also have `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)]` on their T parameter. Additionally, `GenericOperationSource<T>` is instantiated in those methods (around line 89: `new GenericOperationSource<T>(client, isResource)`), and since GenericOperationSource now requires `PublicConstructors | NonPublicConstructors` on T, the callers need to satisfy that too. So:

```csharp
public static ArmOperation<T> Rehydrate<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>(ArmClient client, RehydrationToken rehydrationToken, ArmClientOptions options = null) where T : notnull
```

And similarly for the async version `RehydrateAsync<T>`.

Make sure `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` is present in both files.

## 3. ArmClientBuilderExtensions.cs

Line 30 calls `builder.RegisterClientFactory<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions>(configuration)` which has `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]` and `[RequiresDynamicCode]`.

Fix: Add `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]` and `[RequiresDynamicCode]` to the `AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>` method:
```csharp
[RequiresUnreferencedCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values is not supported with trimming. Use the Configuration Binder Source Generator (EnableConfigurationBindingGenerator=true) instead.")]
[RequiresDynamicCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values requires generating dynamic code at runtime, for example instantiating generic types.")]
public static IAzureClientBuilder<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions> AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>(this TBuilder builder, TConfiguration configuration)
```

Make sure `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` is present.

## 4. ArmEnvironment.cs

Line 80: `public override string ToString() => JsonSerializer.Serialize(this);`

Replace with manual JSON construction:
```csharp
public override string ToString()
{
    return $"{{\"Endpoint\":\"{Endpoint}\",\"Audience\":\"{Audience}\",\"DefaultScope\":\"{DefaultScope}\"}}";
}
```

No need to import anything new, just remove the `using System.Text.Json;` if it's only used for this.

Wait, check if `using System.Text.Json;` is used elsewhere. If not, you can remove it. If it is, leave it.

## 5. ArmClientOptions.cs

Line 52: `var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);`

Replace with JsonDocument-based parsing:
```csharp
using (JsonDocument doc = JsonDocument.Parse(BinaryData.FromStream(stream)))
```

The full replacement for lines 51-53 should be:
```csharp
var data = BinaryData.FromStream(stream);
using var doc = JsonDocument.Parse(data);
var armProfile = doc.RootElement.GetProperty("resource-manager");
foreach (var namespaceProperty in armProfile.EnumerateObject())
{
    var namespaceName = namespaceProperty.Name;
    foreach (var apiVersionProperty in namespaceProperty.Value.EnumerateObject())
    {
        var apiVersion = apiVersionProperty.Name;
        foreach (var resourceTypeItem in apiVersionProperty.Value.EnumerateArray())
        {
            string resourceTypeName = default;
            foreach (var property in resourceTypeItem.EnumerateObject())
            {
                if (property.NameEquals("resourceType"))
                {
                    resourceTypeName = property.Value.GetString();
                    break;
                }
            }
            var resourceType = $"{namespaceName}/{resourceTypeName}";
            ResourceApiVersionOverrides[resourceType] = apiVersion;
        }
    }
}
```

This replaces the entire nested loop structure from lines 51-77 (from `var span =` through the end of the loops). The key change is removing `JsonSerializer.Deserialize` and using `JsonDocument.Parse` + `GetProperty` instead, and removing the unused `span` variable.

After this change, check if `using System.Collections.Generic;` is still needed (it is, for `Dictionary`/`IDictionary`). Also check if `using System.Text.Json;` is still needed (it should be, for `JsonDocument`/`JsonElement`).

